  "prompt": "A charming charcoal-black miniature top hat with a short square brim, tall blocky crown and a deep red ribbon painted around the crown. A clean formal silhouette, subtle charcoal pixel shading. No extra badges or floating details. This is an equippable hat for tiny real-animal pets in vanilla Minecraft. Create the original hat ONLY, without a pet, stand, background or text. Fit all geometry within x=2..14, z=2..14, y=0..14, centred horizontally at x=z=8, flat wearable underside exactly y=0, facing negative Z. Use 4-16 purposeful unrotated axis-aligned cuboids, not voxels or smooth curves. Single compact shared painted cube-net atlas, one texel per model unit; explicit integer uvSize for any fractional geometry. No bones or animation. Connected robust forms, no z-fighting. Distinct Minecraft-style inventory silhouette. This will be uniformly scaled to each animal head with the bottom resting on its forehead; do not model straps, hair, ears or a head.",
